\textbf{Reproducibility.} Run \texttt{python3 verification.py}; the complete output and preregistration are included. \textbf{Data and code availability.} The package contains all generated code and uses no private data. \textbf{Funding.} No external funding is declared. \textbf{Conflicts of interest.} The author declares no conflict specific to this note. \textbf{Authorship accountability.} Justin D. Hart is the accountable author. \textbf{AI-use disclosure.} Codex performed standards review, literature search, model checking, code execution, drafting, and packaging under human direction. Historical Viridis artifacts attributable to Claude were consulted without rewriting their authorship.

\section{Conclusion}
A declared thermodynamic benefit ledger plus smooth transition friction and one budget yields an auditable clipped shadow-price allocation. The method is reproducible and non-vacuous but deliberately remains an internal methods note because established replacement and convex-allocation literature limits the demonstrated delta.

